00:27:05.630 --> 00:27:08.330
too, ways for people
to link in and find out

00:27:08.330 --> 00:27:09.599
how to get involved.

00:27:09.599 --> 00:27:11.390
I want to make sure,
is there anything else

00:27:11.390 --> 00:27:13.760
that you wanted to share
or talk about, you know,

00:27:13.760 --> 00:27:16.870
from AI, from the research,
from recommendations for people

00:27:16.870 --> 00:27:18.600
to think about how
they get involved,

00:27:18.600 --> 00:27:20.000
how they can get into the space?

00:27:20.000 --> 00:27:22.290
FEI-FEI LI: AI is
incredibly exciting.

00:27:22.290 --> 00:27:27.380
I guess I'm biased, but being
a AI technologist and also

00:27:27.380 --> 00:27:30.290
educator for 20
years, I think seeing

00:27:30.290 --> 00:27:33.650
this field has grown from
a niche academic field

00:27:33.650 --> 00:27:35.720
to become one of
the biggest drivers

00:27:35.720 --> 00:27:38.150
of the fourth
Industrial Revolution

00:27:38.150 --> 00:27:41.210
is really extremely
exciting and rewarding.

00:27:41.210 --> 00:27:45.480
And in this process I think
we are just at the beginning,

00:27:45.480 --> 00:27:49.640
even though we hear a lot about
AI and its progress so far.

00:27:49.640 --> 00:27:52.850
But we really are just seeing
the beginning of the power

00:27:52.850 --> 00:27:54.000
of this technology.

00:27:54.000 --> 00:27:57.800
So I would love to see more
people getting involved,

00:27:57.800 --> 00:28:01.590
and different parts of
the world, technologies,

00:28:01.590 --> 00:28:04.970
technologists,
humanists, policymakers,

00:28:04.970 --> 00:28:08.420
social scientists, you
know, lawmakers all

00:28:08.420 --> 00:28:13.610
come together and have deeper
and multi-way dialogue,

00:28:13.610 --> 00:28:16.850
and to design this
technology, and also guide

00:28:16.850 --> 00:28:18.614
the impact of this technology.

